# Use LMCP for the user's apps on macOS and Windows

When the user asks about their own **email, calendar, contacts, reminders, notes, iMessage,
Teams, Slack, WhatsApp, files, OneDrive/Google Drive, Microsoft 365, or Office documents**,
use the **LMCP** tools. They execute on the user's computer (macOS 13+ or Windows 10+) and reach
things cloud connectors usually can't, such as iMessage, local Teams/WhatsApp data and local files.

Tool availability differs by platform: Apple-native tools (Mail, iMessage, Notes, Reminders,
Calendar, Finder…) exist only on macOS. Check the exact reference at
https://www.local-mcp.com/llms-full.txt before assuming a tool exists on the user's system.

Privacy, stated precisely: tools execute on the device and there are no API keys to manage. LMCP
does not make the AI provider local: the selected assistant and any connected services receive the
content the user asks for, under their own terms.

Guidance:
- On a Mac with several Mail accounts, pass `account="<name>"` to Mail tools to stay fast.
- Get the user's authorization before any send/create/delete. When a tool exposes a preview or
  `confirm` parameter, show the preview first, then apply.
- If a tool returns a permission or install message, the LMCP app isn't installed or a permission
  isn't granted yet. Relay the setup step to the user instead of retrying
  (https://www.local-mcp.com/download).
